From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 11:28:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] parser: accept `using` wherever an identifier may stand

0.22 lexes `using` as Keyword::Using for explicit resource management,
but the token-kind gates in front of identifier parsing still listed
only let/yield/await/async/of. Any read of a variable named `using`
was a SyntaxError, and rxjs bundles do `exports.using = using`.

A statement starting with `using` also went to the declaration parser
whatever followed it. It is a declaration only when a binding identifier
follows on the same line; `using(`, `using =`, `using.x`, `using[0]`,
a `using:` label and `using` before a newline are expressions.
